{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
They [Bb]traveled through the island to Paphos [F/A]town
Where a ma[Gm]gician named Bar-Je-sus was [Eb]found
With the [Bb]proconsul Sergius Pau[F/A]lus he stayed
An in[Gm]telligent man in [Eb]the ancient way
[Cm]He sent for Barnabas and Saul to [F]come
Eager to [Cm]hear the word of God in the [F]room
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Eager to hear [Bb]the word of God
Sergius [F/A]Paulus sought the living Lord
When the pro[Gm]consul saw what had been [Eb]done
He believed in the light that [Bb]was won
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
But Elymas the magician stood in the [F/A]way
Trying [Gm]to turn the proconsul from the [Eb]day
He op[Bb]posed them with his tricks of old
[F/A]Seeking to stop the story to be told
Then [Gm]Saul filled with the Spirit [Eb]looked at him straight
And de[Cm7]clared the judgment from God’s own [F]gate
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Dm]A mist and darkness came [Eb]over his eyes
[Dm]He groped for hands in the sur[Eb]prise
[Dm]Twisting the straight paths of the [Eb]Lord he tried
But the [Cm7]hand of the Lord was his [F]guide
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Eager to hear [Bb]the word of God
Sergius Pau[F/A]lus sought the living Lord
When the pro[Gm]consul saw what had been [Eb]done
He believed in the light that was [Bb]won
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
As[F/A]tounded at the teaching of the [Gm]Lord
[Eb]He came to faith with a heart trans[Bb]formed
{end_of_verse}

